    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Freeman** (60.09) and **Gavin Sheets** (59.95) stand out as our most reliable offensive anchors. **Tyler Freeman** benefits from a substantial +14% park factor adjustment and a favorable matchup against the occasionally erratic Freddy Peralta, with his high sprint speed offering a distinct edge in our scarcity-focused strategy. Meanwhile, **Gavin Sheets** draws a prime matchup against Houser; his +14% SP skill adjustment highlights the exploitable nature of this duel, elevating him to the top of our lineup. **Cal Raleigh** (74.56) remains the highest-projected player on the board, as his dynamic platoon advantage against P\u00e9rez and the structural importance of the #2 spot provide a massive floor, even with a slight park-induced drag.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Daulton Varsho** on the bench. While his profile typically fits our aggressive SB-chase model\u2014aided by a +2% bump for facing a slow-delivery pitcher\u2014his confirmed absence from the starting lineup resulted in an automatic exclusion. We are also navigating a significant talent bottleneck; facing top-tier arms like Skenes, Ragans, and Wheeler forced defensive scoring adjustments for **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, and **Lawrence Butler**. Despite the elite pedigree of those opposing pitchers, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** maintains a respectable 55.69, bolstered by the reliability of the #3 hole. Conversely, **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Jonathan Aranda** face uphill climbs against Skenes and Corbin, respectively, requiring disciplined management of our game caps.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in our heavy exposure to high-strikeout environments. While **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a favorable wind-out condition and a +13% platoon edge, he is essentially facing an elite arm in Wheeler; his 51.42 score is a testament to the fact that his aggressive profile is being tempered by the matchup quality. We remain vigilant regarding **Yainer Diaz**, who remains sidelined on the IL, alongside **Bryson Stott**, **Will Smith**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Wenceel Perez**, and **Drew Gilbert**, all of whom are unavailable today due to roster status or rest. Owners should monitor the late-afternoon weather, though no immediate rainouts are projected to threaten these matchups.",
